 34b143f7637ca2730c1c { --sqs-block-content-flex: 0\; } #block-34b143f7637c
 a2730c1c { --opacity: 100%\; --translate-x: 0px\; --translate-y: 0px\; --r
 otation: 0deg\; --scale-x: 100%\; --scale-y: 100%\; --skew-x: 0deg\; --ske
 w-y: 0deg\; --origin-x: 50%\; --origin-y: 50%\; --block-transform: none\; 
 opacity: var(--opacity\, 1)\; transform: var(--block-transform)\; transfor
 m-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } Discover a simple yet powerf
 ul approach to painting by focusing on the three essential elements of suc
 cessful artwork: drawing\, value\, and color. In this two-day workshop\, G
 eorge will guide students through the fundamentals of composition and draw
 ing\, including how to create a strong focal point\, measure proportions a
 ccurately\, and lead the viewer's eye through a painting. Next\, participa
 nts will explore the critical role of value by painting with only Ultramar
 ine Blue and White\, learning how light and dark relationships create dept
 h\, form\, and visual impact. Finally\, students will unlock the secrets o
 f color harmony using only the three primary colors and white\, mixing a w
 ide range of vibrant palettes while exploring warm and cool color relation
 ships\, color temperature\, and atmospheric perspective. Through demonstra
 tions and a series of color studies\, this workshop provides artists of al
 l levels with practical tools for creating stronger\, more confident paint
 ings. This is an intermediate painting&nbsp\;class. Students will be asked
  to bring their own material. A list of required material will be provided
  to all students upon sign up. This class is located in the PAC classroom.
 &nbsp\; Two days\, 12-4PM each day. About the Teacher:&nbsp\; George Scrib
 ner i s an artist\, filmmaker\, and longtime Disney animator\, director\, 
 and fine artist with more than 35 years at The Walt Disney Company. Born a
 nd raised in Panama\, he directed Disney's animated feature&nbsp\; Oliver 
 &amp\; Company &nbsp\;and has earned international recognition for his lar
 ge-scale documentary paintings. His major commissions include creating 35 
 oil paintings chronicling the expansion of the Panama Canal for its perman
 ent collection and a multi-year series documenting the construction of Sha
 nghai Disneyland. Through his work\, George combines masterful draftsmansh
 ip\, storytelling\, and a lifelong passion for painting and animation. Lea
 rn More:&nbsp\; www.scribnerart.com #block-aba7662773e72679cc5e { --stroke
